= Adaptation (systems) — Technical =

== Adaptive update ==
A generic adaptive system can be written as:

<pre>
state x_t
parameters/policy θ_t
environment e_t

θ_(t+1) = F(θ_t, x_t, e_t, feedback_t)
</pre>

where F can represent learning, selection, control, reconfiguration, or other update dynamics.

== Timescales ==
Adaptation can occur across:

* fast control timescales;
* behavioral/learning timescales;
* developmental/organizational timescales;
* evolutionary timescales.

Separating timescales can be essential for analysis.

== Coevolution ==
When adaptive components alter one another's environments, the system may exhibit coevolution:

<pre>
agent adaptation ↔ environment/other-agent change
</pre>

This can create path dependence and moving fitness/objective landscapes.

